# Python server discipline

Follow the project's existing framework, package layout, and async/sync conventions
before adding endpoints, services, or data-access code.

Validate external input at API boundaries using the same pydantic, serializer, or
form patterns the codebase already uses.

Use parameterized queries or the project's ORM — never build SQL with string
concatenation from user input.

Match existing typing style: add type hints when the surrounding modules use them;
do not introduce a conflicting style in one file.

Prefer the project's configured virtual environment and dependency manifests —
do not assume global packages.

Do not add heavyweight dependencies when an existing project library already
covers the need.
